WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.242 --> 00:00:18.166
I asked Buck whether any Grangerfords and Shepherdsons had been killed in the past few months.

2
00:00:18.186 --> 00:00:23.568
"Oh, yes," he replied calmly, "one of ours and one of theirs.

3
00:00:24.609 --> 00:00:26.009
We have a lot of funerals."

4
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:31.271
He went on to tell me that both his brothers and his father had been wounded in battles

5
00:00:31.352 --> 00:00:32.232
with the Shepherdsons.

6
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.182
On Sunday, I went to church with the Grangerfords.

7
00:00:37.383 --> 00:00:43.749
The sermon was about brotherly love, but all the Grangerford men had their guns with them, and so

8
00:00:43.789 --> 00:00:44.770
did the Shepherdson men.

9
00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.953
It was the strangest church service I had ever attended.

10
00:00:51.355 --> 00:00:56.980
Later that afternoon, when I was going upstairs to my room, Miss Sophia came out of her room.

11
00:00:58.061 --> 00:01:01.744
She told me in a whisper that she had forgotten her Bible in the church.

12
00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:05.402
"Would you please go to the church and get it for me?"

13
00:01:06.062 --> 00:01:06.483
she said.

14
00:01:07.303 --> 00:01:09.785
Then she added, "Please don't tell anyone."

15
00:01:11.106 --> 00:01:17.090
I found the book, but it seemed odd that Miss Sophia was so nervous about a Bible, so

16
00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:19.592
I shook it to see if anything was inside.

17
00:01:20.612 --> 00:01:23.334
A note fluttered out that said, "Two-thirty."

18
00:01:24.955 --> 00:01:30.199
I tucked the note back in the Bible and, when I returned, gave the book to Miss Sophia

19
00:01:30.379 --> 00:01:31.460
without saying anything.

20
00:01:32.496 --> 00:01:36.039
She gave me a hug and told me I was the best boy in the world.

21
00:01:37.921 --> 00:01:40.703
Later I decided to go for a walk by the river.

22
00:01:41.704 --> 00:01:46.447
I soon noticed that one of the house slaves, a man named Jack, was following me.

23
00:01:47.368 --> 00:01:51.111
He asked me if I'd like to go down to the swamp and see some snakes.

24
00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:56.055
I thought this was strange, but I agreed and followed him into the swamp.

25
00:01:57.436 --> 00:02:01.640
We were ankle-deep in water for a while, and then we came to a dry place.

26
00:02:02.728 --> 00:02:06.010
Jack said that I should go ahead while he went back to the house.

27
00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:11.552
I took a few steps, pushing aside some vines, and there was Jim!

28
00:02:12.372 --> 00:02:13.653
I was so happy to see him.

29
00:02:15.093 --> 00:02:19.155
Jim explained that he had managed to swim to shore a little while after I did.

30
00:02:20.176 --> 00:02:23.337
When he saw me go into the house, he hid in the woods nearby.

31
00:02:24.418 --> 00:02:29.300
The next day, he went up to some of the Grangerfords' slaves working in the fields and asked

32
00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:29.800
for their help.

33
00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:33.221
They showed him a hiding place in the swamp.

34
00:02:34.141 --> 00:02:36.561
And then Jim told me the best news of all.

35
00:02:37.382 --> 00:02:40.663
The raft hadn't been completely destroyed by the steamboat.

36
00:02:41.663 --> 00:02:45.784
He'd been repairing it, and it would be ready for travel in a couple of days.

37
00:02:48.205 --> 00:02:51.766
When I woke up the next morning, the house was strangely quiet.

38
00:02:52.806 --> 00:02:55.967
I went downstairs and Jack told me the terrible news.

39
00:02:57.127 --> 00:03:01.268
Miss Sophia had run away to marry Harney Shepherdson.

40
00:03:01.288 --> 00:03:07.370
The Grangerford women had gone to a relative's house to get more help, while Colonel Grangerford and his

41
00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.671
three sons had rode off with their guns.

42
00:03:11.411 --> 00:03:14.692
They intended to kill Harney and bring Miss Sophia back.

43
00:03:16.112 --> 00:03:21.114
I ran down the road after them as fast as I could, and before long I heard shooting.

44
00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:27.456
I snuck through the trees until I came to the riverbank near a store that sold supplies to

45
00:03:27.516 --> 00:03:28.816
people traveling on the river.

46
00:03:30.648 --> 00:03:34.792
Men were shooting at each other along the shore and from inside the store.

47
00:03:35.792 --> 00:03:40.456
I could see Buck and an older boy who was his cousin hiding behind a big woodpile.

48
00:03:41.537 --> 00:03:45.800
It was too dangerous to stay where I was, so I climbed a tree and hid there.

49
00:03:47.722 --> 00:03:52.546
I saw several men shot dead on both sides, and then the Shepherdson men rode away.

50
00:03:53.647 --> 00:03:55.208
I called out to Buck from the tree.

51
00:03:56.672 --> 00:04:01.734
Crying and cursing the Shepherdsons, he told me that his father and both his older brothers had been

52
00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:08.916
killed. I asked Buck what had happened to Harney and Miss Sophia, and he said they had gotten

53
00:04:08.956 --> 00:04:14.717
away. He asked me to stay in the tree and watch for the Shepherdsons to ride back, and

54
00:04:14.757 --> 00:04:15.458
I said I would.

55
00:04:16.238 --> 00:04:18.318
But suddenly gunfire broke out again.

56
00:04:19.299 --> 00:04:23.080
The Shepherdsons had circled back and snuck up on Buck and his cousin.

57
00:04:24.852 --> 00:04:29.015
What happened next made me feel so sick I almost fell out of the tree.

58
00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:31.957
I still have nightmares about it.

59
00:04:32.678 --> 00:04:35.040
The Shepherdsons killed Buck and his cousin.

60
00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:36.601
Then they fled.

61
00:04:37.582 --> 00:04:42.165
I was so scared that I waited until it was dark before I climbed down from the tree.

62
00:04:43.426 --> 00:04:45.868
I never wanted to see the Grangerford house again.

63
00:04:47.789 --> 00:04:51.112
I blamed myself because I had brought the note to Miss Sophia.

64
00:04:52.088 --> 00:04:55.231
Maybe if she hadn't received it, she wouldn't have run away.

65
00:04:56.312 --> 00:05:00.675
I ran back to the dry spot in the swamp to find Jim—but he wasn't there!

66
00:05:01.936 --> 00:05:04.638
I scrambled down to the riverbank, yelling his name.

67
00:05:05.659 --> 00:05:09.042
Then I heard a soft voice: "Is that you, Huck?

68
00:05:09.583 --> 00:05:10.723
Don't make any noise."

69
00:05:12.285 --> 00:05:15.948
It was Jim's voice—and nothing had ever sounded so good to me.

70
00:05:17.084 --> 00:05:21.868
I ran a little way along the bank until I came to the raft and scrambled aboard.

71
00:05:22.948 --> 00:05:24.109
Jim and I hugged each other.

72
00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:26.931
Once again, he had thought I was dead.

73
00:05:27.772 --> 00:05:31.174
Jack had told him about the gun battle, and that I hadn't come home.

74
00:05:31.194 --> 00:05:35.597
"Let's just leave, Jim, as fast as we can," I said.

75
00:05:37.199 --> 00:05:41.301
When we were about three kilometers down the river, I began to feel safer.

76
00:05:42.362 --> 00:05:44.604
We hung up our lantern and ate some supper.

77
00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:50.488
I was very happy to get away from the feud, and Jim was happy to get away from

78
00:05:50.529 --> 00:05:51.009
the swamp.

79
00:05:51.971 --> 00:05:54.655
We agreed there was no home as good as our raft.
